.TH YKING 1 2026-11-27 "yking" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yking \- set up YubiKeys on Linux: SSH, PAM, LUKS, PGP, KeePassXC, plug/unplug actions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yking
.RB [ \-keyring
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B yking
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without a command,
.B yking
starts an interactive terminal interface (TUI) that runs as the user.
Every change to system files is shown as a diff first and applied with
.BR sudo (8)
only after confirmation; changes to the user's own files are applied
without root.
Each apply keeps backups and can be undone with
.BR "yking rollback" .
.PP
yking never resets a YubiKey, never changes PINs and writes only into
empty slots (see
.BR SAFETY ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR detect " [" \-\-json ]
Read-only inventory of the connected keys.
.TP
.B doctor
Read-only health check of the whole setup. Exits 1 on errors.
.TP
.BR apply " [" \-\-yes "] " \fIPLAN\fR
Apply a reviewed plan (the TUI does this through
.BR sudo ).
.TP
.B history
List applied plans.
.TP
.BR rollback " [" \-\-user "] [" \-\-force "] [" \-\-yes "] [" \fIID\fR ]
Undo an applied plan (default: the latest).
.B \-\-user
undoes a change to the user's own files and needs no root.
.B \-\-force
restores even if a file changed after yking wrote it.
.TP
.BR export " [" \-o " \fIFILE\fR] [" \-\-no\-ssh ]
Export the setup for another machine.
.TP
.BI import " FILE"
Stage an export; finish it in the TUI with
.BR i .
.TP
.B luks status
LUKS volumes, keyslots and the boot unlock method.
.TP
.BR "luks enroll" " [" \-\-device " \fIDEV\fR] [" \-\-unlock " " pin+touch | touch ]
Add a key as a FIDO2 keyslot. Plugged in alone, the passphrase or recovery
key authorizes it; plugged in next to an already enrolled key, that key
does (PIN and touch), so a disk without passphrase can get new keys.
.TP
.BR "luks migrate" " [" \-\-dry\-run ]
Switch the initramfs to systemd unlocking (needed for FIDO2 at boot).
.TP
.B luks repair
Rebuild the boot files after a failed migration.
.TP
.BR "luks identify" " [" \-\-record ]
Find which keyslot belongs to the plugged-in key.
.TP
.BI "luks wipe \-\-slot " N\fR[,\fIM\fR...] " \fR[" "\-\-device " DEV\fR]
Remove FIDO2 keyslots from the disk (the passphrase or recovery key stays).
On a disk without passphrase, one plugged-in enrolled key authorizes it;
its own slot cannot be removed.
.TP
.BR "luks backup" " [" \-\-device " \fIDEV\fR] [" \-\-out " \fIDIR\fR]"
Save the LUKS header in
.I /var/lib/yking/luks
and, with
.BR \-\-out ,
copy it into a folder off this disk (that one belongs to the user).
Both copies are verified.
.TP
.B luks passphrase remove
Remove the passphrase of the root volume and replace it with a recovery
key (shown once) or nothing (key-only). Only when boot unlocks with FIDO2,
two registered keys are enrolled and the plugged-in key has just unlocked
the volume the way boot does. Key-only: losing every key loses the data; adding a key then needs an
enrolled key plugged in next to the new one.
.TP
.BR event " " add | remove | status
Plug/unplug handler run by
.BR yking-event@.service ;
.B status
shows the configuration.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH TUI
The key list shows connected and registered keys. Keys:
.TP
.B e
Register the selected key.
.TP
.B t
Silent key test (no touch).
.TP
.B c
Check the key's PAM credential; add one.
.TP
.BR s ", " l ", " d
Create an SSH key on the key, link an existing one, deploy it to servers.
.TP
.B o
Manage yking's
.B Host
blocks in
.IR ~/.ssh/config .
.TP
.B p
PAM per service: off, key or password, key and password, key only.
.TP
.B g
PGP: list GnuPG identities, create one, add a signing subkey, copy the
signing and encryption subkeys to the plugged-in key, back them up,
set git signing, remove them from disk (card-only).
.TP
.B v
KeePassXC: write one HMAC-SHA1 challenge-response secret into OTP slot 2
of each key.
.TP
.B b
Disk: LUKS FIDO2 enrollment, boot switch, header backup, passphrase removal.
.TP
.B u
Plug/unplug actions: lock the screen and reset sudo when the last trigger
key is pulled out; wake the lock screen when a key is plugged in.
.TP
.B x
Revoke a key (lost or replaced).
.TP
.B i
Finish an import.
.TP
.B h
Doctor.
.TP
.B U
Update the installed copy
.RI ( /usr/local/bin/yking )
to this build.
.TP
.B ?
All keys of the current screen.
.PP
Long screens scroll with PgUp/PgDn or the mouse wheel. Select text with
Shift+drag.
.SH PGP
Card writes never happen in
.IR ~/.gnupg .
The subkeys are exported into a throwaway GnuPG home in
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
(must be a tmpfs), moved to the card there, and the throwaway home is
deleted, so the same subkeys can go to every key.
Only empty slots, or slots holding the same fingerprint, are written.
The Admin PIN is asked once and only while at least 2 tries are left.
Touch is set to
.BR on .
.PP
.B f
adds
.B disable-ccid
and
.B pcsc-shared
to
.IR scdaemon.conf ,
so gpg and ykman can share the key.
.SH KEEPASSXC
The secret exists only in memory while the screen is open; write it to
every key in one visit and keep the paper copy
.RB ( p )
to set up a key later
.RB ( i ).
The secret is passed to ykman on stdin, written only into an empty slot 2
and verified with a test challenge.
.B u
installs a udev rule that gives the logged-in user the OTP interface,
which challenge-response over USB needs.
.SH SAFETY
yking runs ykman only through an allowlist without reset, delete, PIN or
interface commands. The one exception is clearing OTP slot 2
.RB ( x
on the KeePassXC screen), offered only for a key whose slot just failed the
challenge-response test, after the key's label was typed.
.PP
Key-only PAM needs at least two registered keys and one service that still
accepts a password. Lock screens always get pam_u2f's
.B interactive
option; lock on unplug is refused, and skipped at run time, while a lock
screen lacks it.
.PP
Locked out of the desktop: press Ctrl+Alt+F2, log in on the console and
run
.BR "loginctl unlock-sessions" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/yking/keyring.toml
Registered keys and what each one holds (no secrets).
.TP
.I /etc/yking/events.toml
Plug/unplug configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/yking/luks-slots.json
Keyslot lists of the LUKS volumes as root last read them (no secrets), for
the disk screen.
.TP
.I /var/lib/yking/backups/
Backups of system files, one directory per applied plan.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/yking/backups/
Backups of the user's own files.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/yking/plans/
Plans waiting for the elevated apply.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/yking
Installed copy, used by the plug/unplug handler.
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/90-yking.rules
.TQ
.I /etc/systemd/system/yking-event@.service
Plug/unplug handler.
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/69-yking-otp.rules
OTP interface access for challenge-response.
.TP
.I /run/yking/
Keys seen by the plug/unplug handler.
.TP
.I ~/.config/Yubico/u2f_keys
pam_u2f credentials.
.TP
.I ~/.gnupg/scdaemon.conf
gpg card access.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Location of the throwaway GnuPG home (tmpfs).
.TP
.B GNUPGHOME
The user's GnuPG home (default
.IR ~/.gnupg ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on errors (for
.BR doctor :
errors found), 2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ykman (1),
.BR gpg (1),
.BR pamu2fcfg (1),
.BR pam_u2f (8),
.BR systemd-cryptenroll (1),
.BR ssh-keygen (1),
.BR keepassxc (1)
